# Known divergence, by design: multigres rejects CREATE FOREIGN DATA WRAPPER
# (Tier-2 — foreign data wrappers / foreign tables are not supported through the
# connection pooler; see go/services/multigateway/planner/unsafe_stmt.go).
# ownership builds an FDW inside a helper function (test_fdw) via a constant
# EXECUTE, so the gateway rejects that helper's CREATE FUNCTION; the missing
# helper then breaks the file's single wrapping transaction, truncating the whole
# tail from that point to finish(). That tail bundles the foreign_table_owner_is
# assertions together with the file's remaining general ownership checks
# (function_owner_is, language_owner_is, materialized_view_owner_is), which are
# emitted after the rejected helper and so are lost with it. The ~200 assertions
# before it (table/view/sequence/type/... _owner_is) run and stay verified.
